<section class="hero">
  <p class="eyebrow">A macOS utility for project workspaces</p>
  <h1>The repository is permanent.<br>The local development environment is disposable.</h1>
  <p class="lede">Your source is small. Your workspace is not. Dormant separates the two: clean what
    can be regenerated, put idle projects to sleep as verified archives, and wake them exactly as
    you left them.</p>
  <div class="hero-actions">
    <span class="button button-primary button-soon">Coming soon for macOS</span>
    <a class="button button-secondary" href="#moves">See how it works</a>
  </div>
  <p class="requirements">macOS 14 or later · Menu bar app with a Finder extension · No account, no network</p>
  <div class="install-block">
    <pre class="install-line"><code>brew tap PrakashSewani/tap &amp;&amp; brew install --cask dormant</code></pre>
    <button class="copy-button" type="button" disabled>Copy</button>
  </div>
  <p class="requirements">Not published yet — this install goes live with the first release.</p>
  <p class="requirements">First launch: System Settings → Privacy &amp; Security → "Open Anyway" (Dormant is ad-hoc signed).</p>
</section>

<section class="proof" aria-labelledby="proof-title">
  <h2 id="proof-title">Where the gigabytes actually are</h2>
  <p class="section-lede">Dormant reads a workspace the way you wish you had: what your tools
    generated is disposable, what you wrote is not.</p>

  <div class="ledger-pair">
    <article class="ledger" aria-label="Workspace sizes before archiving">
      <header class="ledger-head">
        <span class="ledger-title">On disk</span>
        <span class="ledger-total">2.31 GB</span>
      </header>
      <p class="ledger-path">~/Projects/heatmap</p>
      <table class="ledger-table">
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>node_modules/</td><td class="num">2.18 GB</td><td class="kind kind-re">regenerable</td></tr>
          <tr><td>target/</td><td class="num">112 MB</td><td class="kind kind-re">regenerable</td></tr>
          <tr><td>.next/</td><td class="num">41 MB</td><td class="kind kind-re">regenerable</td></tr>
          <tr><td>source, .git, docs, configs</td><td class="num">14.3 MB</td><td class="kind kind-core">core</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p class="ledger-note">Unclassified files are never guessed at. They travel with the archive,
        labeled in the manifest.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="ledger ledger-stored" aria-label="Archive store after archiving">
      <header class="ledger-head">
        <span class="ledger-title">In the store</span>
        <span class="ledger-total">4.9 MB</span>
      </header>
      <p class="ledger-path">~/.dormant/store/6f3b21c4/</p>
      <table class="ledger-table">
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>core.tar.gz</td><td class="num">4.9 MB</td><td class="kind kind-core">421 files</td></tr>
          <tr><td>manifest.json</td><td class="num">96 KB</td><td class="kind kind-core">SHA-256 verified</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p class="ledger-note">The working copy is removed only after the archive passes an entry-set
        check against what it should contain.</p>
    </article>
  </div>

  <details class="manifest">
    <summary>manifest.json</summary>
    <pre><code>{
  "manifestVersion": 1,
  "project": { "name": "heatmap", "originalPath": "/Users/you/Projects/heatmap",
               "ecosystems": ["node", "rust"], "archivedAt": "2026-09-26T08:14:02Z" },
  "git": { "isRepo": true, "branch": "dev", "dirty": false, "modifiedCount": 0 },
  "tarball": { "name": "core.tar.gz", "size": 4912384, "fileCount": 421,
               "sha256": "9f2c…" },
  "files": [ { "path": "src/heatmap.rs", "size": 5821, "kind": "core" },
             { "path": "notes.txt", "size": 412, "kind": "unclassified" } ]
}</code></pre>
  </details>
</section>

<section class="moves" id="moves" aria-labelledby="moves-title">
  <h2 id="moves-title">Three moves</h2>
  <ol class="move-list">
    <li class="move">
      <span class="move-num" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
      <div class="move-body">
        <h3>Clean</h3>
        <p>Remove dependency folders, build output and caches. You see every path with its size
          before anything happens, and only paths classified as regenerable are ever touched.</p>
        <p class="move-safety">A folder it cannot classify stays on disk. Guessing is not a mode.</p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li class="move">
      <span class="move-num" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
      <div class="move-body">
        <h3>Archive</h3>
        <p>Clean, compress everything that remains into a local store, and remove the working copy.
          Days or gigabytes later, the project is one small, verified archive.</p>
        <p class="move-safety">Uncommitted work raises a warning with modified and untracked counts
          before anything is packed.</p>
      </div>
    </li>
    <li class="move move-wake">
      <span class="move-num" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
      <div class="move-body">
        <h3>Restore</h3>
        <p>Unpack to the original path, verify every file against the manifest checksums, and show
          the exact install commands before running a single one.</p>
        <p class="move-safety">If verification fails, the archive stays put and the extracted tree is
          left for inspection.</p>
      </div>
    </li>
  </ol>

  <div class="restore-proof">
    <p class="restore-label">What Restore shows before it runs anything</p>
    <pre><code>Restore  ~/Projects/heatmap
  npm install        package-lock.json
  cargo build        Cargo.toml

Nothing runs until you confirm.</code></pre>
  </div>

  <p class="also">Also in the menu: <strong>Project Info</strong> (local size versus core versus
    regenerable, git status, branch, remote), <strong>Open</strong> in your configured editor, and
    <strong>Open Repository</strong> in the browser.</p>
</section>

<section class="rules" id="rules" aria-labelledby="rules-title">
  <h2 id="rules-title">The rules Dormant will not break</h2>
  <ul class="rule-list">
    <li>A Git repository is never deleted.</li>
    <li>Uncommitted changes are never silently discarded.</li>
    <li>A file it cannot classify is never removed.</li>
    <li>Nothing is cleaned merely for being large.</li>
    <li>Every destructive action is previewed and confirmed in the app.</li>
    <li>Recovery needs no account, no network, no Dormant server.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

